  "title": "Understanding Harmful vs Healthy Parenting Behaviours",
  "content": "Parenting behaviours fall into patterns that either build safety or undermine it. Healthy behaviours include calm communication, consistent boundaries, and emotional availability. Harmful behaviours often come from stress, exhaustion, or repeating what we experienced growing up. These may include yelling, unpredictable reactions, or withdrawing emotionally.\n\nThis lesson helps parents recognise these patterns without shame. Behaviour change begins with awareness, not blame. When parents understand the impact of their actions, they can begin replacing harmful habits with healthier ones.\n\nWe explore how children interpret parental behaviour and how even small shifts—like pausing before responding—can dramatically change the emotional climate of the home.",
  "activities": [
    "Identify one behaviour you want to reduce and one you want to increase. Write down what triggers each behaviour.",
    "Practice a 10‑second pause before responding when you feel stressed."
  ],
  "reflectionQuestions": [
    "What behaviours did you learn growing up that you want to change?",
    "How does stress influence the way you respond to your child?",
    "What healthy behaviour do you want to model more consistently?"
